{"candidates":[{"content":"Extend the grounded extension to a credal semantics: each node carries a probability interval [lo, hi] rather than a Boolean label, and the fixed point is the least fixed point of a monotone operator on a finite lattice of intervals, with acceptance defined as lo > τ for a rational threshold τ. Determinism and polynomial cost hold if the operator is componentwise monotone and each update is arithmetic; but reinstatement becomes a derived inequality that can fail to be monotone across thresholds, and the interval semantics may admit multiple fixed points when the lattice is not a complete lattice, so the skeptical choice must be proven unique.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"4fc07d1cf29c58d033683c556e383aabe27935461f789c1c96f95b42883ae66e"},{"role":"dependence","target":"10d18e6652e2cc898265363af979941f9a08d15f3c48e6b767a83bdc505adf2b"}],"typicality":0.35},{"content":"Define a staged grounded extension parameterized by a discrete clock t: at each stage, suspended nodes may be reopened only if a fresh edge-construction warrant was committed in the previous stage, and the extension is the limit of the stage sequence. This makes suspension a dynamic, revisable state rather than a terminal label, and preserves determinism per stage. The criticism: the limit may not be reached in polynomial time unless the stage count is bounded a priori, and the monotonicity of the sequence across stages (reopening is not monotone) breaks the fixed-point determinism guarantee.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"f5a262c5a6bd74029c9528d1063e7a6b5d96c4ee2e4753c79d6fed6817d3fa9b"},{"role":"dependence","target":"5431feda66e41c92d61607a482c76cb05bd782c10644d596f9f903e82e4e8c2f"}],"typicality":0.25},{"content":"Replace the Boolean suspended label with a proof-object: a suspended node is accompanied by the finite set of defeating arguments that kept it OUT, and any reconsideration must be a polynomial proof-search over that certificate set rather than a relabeling or a fresh edge-construction pass. This strengthens the epistemic status of suspension without altering the fixed point's label set, but it imposes a proof-theoretic obligation that may not be decidable in polynomial time for arbitrary attacker sets, and it makes validity a property of certificates rather than of committed roots.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"5431feda66e41c92d61607a482c76cb05bd782c10644d596f9f903e82e4e8c2f"},{"role":"dependence","target":"f5a262c5a6bd74029c9528d1063e7a6b5d96c4ee2e4753c79d6fed6817d3fa9b"}],"typicality":0.55},{"content":"Allow meta-conjectures about the grounded extension itself (e.g., 'node x is IN', 'node y is OUT') to be embedded as ordinary nodes in a higher stratum, computed by a lexicographic fixed point that runs the base extension first and then the meta-level. Determinism and polynomial cost hold per stratum and the validity of every committed root is preserved by construction; the criticism is that a finite stratification cannot express self-reference or iterated reflection without an infinite hierarchy, and the lexicographic order introduces a non-obvious sensitivity to stratum ordering that the flat semantics never had.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"86232ebf5626efc5d29fb5630b9284af34a93dae63929c770bc111d0c4e4e61a"}],"typicality":0.3},{"content":"Replace integer weights and thresholds with a polynomial-time computable total preorder over attackers, and define the grounded labeling as the fixed point of a monotone operator on the product order where a node is IN iff its most-preferred undefeated attacker is absent. This preserves determinism and polynomial cost, but reinstatement becomes preference-dependent rather than a purely structural derived property, and the choice of preorder is itself an extra commitment that must be validated against the rootedness guarantee.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"4fc07d1cf29c58d033683c556e383aabe27935461f789c1c96f95b42883ae66e"},{"role":"dependence","target":"10d18e6652e2cc898265363af979941f9a08d15f3c48e6b767a83bdc505adf2b"}],"typicality":0.45},{"content":"Augment the grounded extension so that every accepted conjecture carries a minimal set of committed root nodes that entail it, and define acceptance as membership in the maximal fixed point whose per-node provenance sets are all root-valid. This turns validity into a per-node, checkable certificate and strengthens the 'validity of every committed root' guarantee into a constructive provenance property. The criticism: computing minimal entailment sets is generally NP-hard, so the polynomial-cost guarantee is lost unless the provenance computation is restricted to a tractable fragment, and the maximal-fixed-point choice may violate the skeptical minimality that grounded semantics guarantees.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"e093eb8611ff0d96fc197357178adfbf4e9e7c0ba8471f3c76aa9f21a3aea46a"},{"role":"dependence","target":"86232ebf5626efc5d29fb5630b9284af34a93dae63929c770bc111d0c4e4e61a"}],"typicality":0.6}],"simulation_proposals":[]}